sort() needs a comparator that returns a number: negative when the first argument sorts first, positive when the second does, zero when they are equal. This one returned true. A test is not a comparator - 'fn(a, b) { return a < b; }' sorts nothing; use 'fn(a, b) { return a - b; }', or for values that cannot be subtracted, 'fn(a, b) { return a < b ? -1 : (a > b ? 1 : 0); }'
